<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/callmesevda/KR-Project/main/proto-ontology-structure.ttl#DirectMatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The two proverbs share both the tacit lesson and the core image (the same scene or object), even if their source-domain tags are worded differently."@en .
<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/callmesevda/KR-Project/main/proto-ontology-structure.ttl#DirectMatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/callmesevda/KR-Project/main/proto-ontology-structure.ttl> .
<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/callmesevda/KR-Project/main/proto-ontology-structure.ttl#DirectMatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Direct match (same lesson AND same source domain)"@en .
<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/callmesevda/KR-Project/main/proto-ontology-structure.ttl#DirectMatch> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Equiv_PRV-020_PRV-029: 'Chi cerca, trova' (it) and 'Kush kërkon, gjen' (sq), both 'who seeks, finds'" .
